-- title:
--   Naturality of the Igusa labelling at an anchoring index (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q=2$, a nonzero level $M'$ not divisible by $q$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$, let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational affine geometric places whose value at the generating $j$-function lies in the supersingular $j$-set), and let $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ via `hle`. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$ whose residue map is computed by coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series over $A$. Fix an index $\zeta$ (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and families of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$: $\mathrm{OIg}$ indexed by $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ and $\mathrm{OSS}$ indexed by $W$. The hypotheses on these two families are: $\mathrm{OIg}$ at the line $\infty$ consists of the quotients $x/y$ of Laurent series over $A$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction; every $\mathrm{OIg}\,\ell$ is the pullback of $\mathrm{OIg}(\infty)$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ carrying $\infty$ to $\ell$ under $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma$; $\mathrm{OIg}$ is injective and is permuted by pullback along every $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; each $\mathrm{OSS}\,s$ meets $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in exactly $A$, is fixed by all such pullbacks, contains an element $t$ with $t-a$ a unit for every $a\in A$, and is compatible with $R_0$ and the place $s$ in the sense that a function of $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ regular wherever the image of $jq$ is, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, lands in $\mathrm{OSS}\,s$, with $f-a$ in the maximal ideal whenever the reduction of $a\in A$ is the value of that residue at $s$. Finally let $\mathcal{C}$ be a `SemistableCovering` for $q,M',A,W$ such that the integers of each Igusa chart $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CIg}\,\ell$ are $\mathrm{OIg}\,\ell$; such that for $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ ($\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$), equality of the integers of $(\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CIg}\,\ell).\mathrm{comap}\,\tau$ and of $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CIg}\,\ell$ forces equality of their domains; such that any permutation $\sigma$ of $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ realising the pullback action on $\mathrm{OIg}$ also transports the annuli $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{An}$ (equal domains after pullback, equal moduli); and satisfying $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{EquivClauses}$. The conclusion is that there is an index $\zeta_0$ such that for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every line $\ell$, pullback along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta_0\,\gamma^{-1}$ takes $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CIg}\,\ell$ to a chart with the same integers and the same domain as $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CIg}((\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma)^{-1}\cdot\ell)$, and takes each annulus $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{An}\,\ell\,s$ to one with the same domain as $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{An}((\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma)^{-1}\cdot\ell)\,s$.
--
--   This is the naturality clause of the assembly of the semistable covering of the full-level modular curve in residue characteristic $2$: it pins down one index $\zeta_0$ for which the permutation of Igusa components and supersingular tube annuli induced by the level automorphisms is exactly the action of $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma)^{-1}$ on $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$. It feeds the existence theorem [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted_of_eq_two_of_dvd), and uses the composition law [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelAutBar_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelAutBar_mul) together with the Borel-stability statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.comap_levelAutBar_eq_of_redQ_smul_lineInfty_eq_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.comap_levelAutBar_eq_of_redQ_smul_lineInfty_eq_of_eq_two) for the Gauss ring.
